### auth-update-profile — happy path: update name only
### auth: protect (any authenticated user); story: US4 / FR-011
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/auth/update-profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Medhat A. Atef"
}

# expect 200
# {
#   "success": true,
#   "data": { "_id": "...", "name": "Medhat A. Atef", "email": "<unchanged>", "phone": null, "avatar": null, "role": "admin", ... }
# }


### auth-update-profile — happy path: update name + phone + avatar
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/auth/update-profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Medhat A. Atef",
  "phone": "+201001112222",
  "avatar": "https://cdn.example.com/avatars/medhat.png"
}

# expect 200 with all three fields persisted


### auth-update-profile — no-op: email equal to current (case-insensitive)
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/auth/update-profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Medhat",
  "email": "MEDHATATEF2004@GMAIL.COM"
}

# expect 200 — email field is treated as no-op when value matches current (case-insensitive); name is persisted


### auth-update-profile — REJECTED: email change attempt (FR-011a)
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/auth/update-profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Medhat",
  "email": "different@example.com"
}

# expect 400
# {
#   "success": false,
#   "message": "email changes require the email-verification flow (not yet available)"
# }
# CRITICAL: name MUST NOT be persisted (atomic rejection per SC-005a)


### auth-update-profile — unauthenticated
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/auth/update-profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "X"
}

# expect 401


### auth-update-profile — empty body
PATCH http://localhost:5000/api/auth/update-profile
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

# expect 400 — Joi schema requires .min(1) (at least one writable field)
